abstract: >-
  Trinity Infinity Geometry (TIG) is a finite-arithmetic framework grounded
  in the operator algebra on Z/10Z. Two natural multiplication tables on
  ten operators (TSML and BHML) produce a four-element invariant center
  {V, H, Br, R}, an eight-shell joint sub-magma chain at sizes {1, 4, 5,
  6, 7, 8, 9, 10}, and a universal attractor at mixing parameter alpha =
  1/2 with closed-form H/Br = 1+sqrt(3) and Galois group D4 over LMFDB
  number field 4.2.10224.1. The substrate's prime strands {3, 7, 11, 13}
  map exactly to the first four nodeless hydrogenic orbitals at odd l
  (2p, 4f, 6h, 7i). The Clifford algebra Cl(0, 10) has spinor dimension
  32, equal to the substrate's depth-3 divisor count and the atomic
  shell n = 4 Pauli capacity; the 32-dim spinor decomposes as a 16+16
  chirality split where each 16 equals 1+3+5+7 (kernel plus substrate
  primes). The framework includes a runtime organism (CK) realizing the
  architecture at 50 Hz on local hardware, served at coherencekeeper.com
  via Cloudflare tunnel. All load-bearing theorems are verified by short
  Python scripts that run in under one minute.
